          "source_errors": [
            "No unique complete structured inactive club list",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: Wide receiver Malik Nabers has not played in a game since suffering a season-ending knee injury on Sept. 28, 2025. He practiced fully all week and was listed as questionable heading into Sunday night. Nabers is active for Week 1.",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: Nabers, who broke the franchise\u2019s single-season reception record as a rookie, was the only Giants player with a game designation on the final injury report.",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: Defensive lineman Shelby Harris (Achilles), offensive lineman Bryan Hudson (knee), tight end Theo Johnson (shoulder) and left tackle Andrew Thomas (knee) were also full participants all week. Fullback Patrick Ricard, a six-time Pro Bowl selection, was added on Friday with a toe injury but was cleared to play.",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: On Saturday, the Giants signed wide receiver Dalen Cambre from the practice squad to the active roster. They also elevated recently-signed linebacker Malik Harrison and wide receiver Braxton Berrios, who is expected to be the Giants\u2019 punt returner.",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: \u201cThe plan with Berrios is treat him like he's playing on the 53,\u201d coach John Harbaugh said the day after they released the veteran when the initial 53-man roster was set. \u201cWe have an opportunity, the way that you can work the roster now, to do that. And that's the plan.\u201d",
            "Unparsed inactive-list line: For the Cowboys, Malik Davis, who figured to be the No. 2 running back behind starter Javonte Williams, suffered a season-ending hip injury on Friday that will require surgery. They subsequently signed running back Israel Abanikanda to the active roster from their practice squad."
          ]
